@{h1}Variadic Functions

From v3 is the additions is support for variadic functions, functions that 
accept a variable number of arguments. Think printf.

In fact, the standard library now includes a lightweight printf 
implementation supporting %c, %s, %d, %x, %X, and %b.

Example Code:

int sum(int count, ...) {
  va_list args;
  int total = 0;
  
  va_start(args, count);
  while (count--) total += va_arg(args, int);
  va_end(args);

  return total;
}
